---
import LegalPage from '../layouts/LegalPage.astro';
import Fill from '../components/Fill.astro';
import { OWNER } from '../config/legal';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy notice"
  description="What B2BRated collects when you visit, who sees it and how to use your rights."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    This site, b2brated.com, is run by <Fill value={OWNER.legalName} label="legal name" />, based in{' '}
    <Fill value={OWNER.country} label="country" />. Contact: <Fill value={OWNER.email} label="contact email" />.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>
    The site has no accounts, no forms, no comments and no advertising. If you accept analytics in the banner, Google
    Analytics records the pages you view and general technical details of your visit. If you decline, we set no
    analytics cookies. The only personal data we hold is what you send us yourself, such as the email address and
    message you write to us, and the host logs described below.
  </p>
  <p>
    We keep emails you send us for as long as needed to answer them and to keep a record of any corrections. We do not
    sell personal data, and we do not share it with anyone except the service providers that run this site.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    Google Tag Manager loads on every page. It starts Google Analytics only after you click Accept analytics. Google
    handles that data under its own privacy policy, and we use it only to see which pages are read. You can decline at
    any time on the <a href="/cookies">cookie policy</a> page, and the data is not used to identify you.
  </p>

  <h2>What our host logs</h2>
  <p>
    Pages are served by Vercel. When you load a page, Vercel receives your IP address, your browser type and the page
    you asked for, and keeps logs to deliver the site and keep it secure. We do not use these logs to identify you. We
    have not set a retention period of our own. Vercel decides how long the logs are kept, and its data may be handled
    outside your country.
  </p>

  <h2>Why this is allowed</h2>
  <p>
    For visitors in the UK and EU, the basis for host logs is our legitimate interest in running a secure website. Any
    website needs a host that logs requests to stay secure. The basis for Google Analytics is your consent, which you
    give or withhold in the banner.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    If you are in the UK or EU you can ask what we hold about you, ask us to correct or delete it, and object to how we
    use it. Email <Fill value={OWNER.email} label="contact email" />. You can also complain to your data protection
    authority. In the UK that is the Information Commissioner's Office.
  </p>

  <h2>When this changes</h2>
  <p>
    We plan to add reviews, vendor accounts and lead requests. Each one collects personal data, so each needs a fuller
    notice before it starts. We will publish the new notice first and change the date at the top of this page.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
